WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.061
One O U tree holds four
different populations,

2
00:00:03.061 --> 00:00:07.975
and they move by different paths, so
the workbook treats them as four tracks.

3
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:11.882
People are the HR track: this
book builds the directory side,

4
00:00:11.882 --> 00:00:16.188
and HR-Driven Identity decides
where their attributes come from.

5
00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:20.453
Devices and servers are the Intune
and Arc tracks: this book's Group

6
00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:25.338
Policy analysis finds their settings,
and Devices and Endpoints moves them.

7
00:00:25.338 --> 00:00:29.991
Service accounts are the non-person
track: this book gives every one

8
00:00:29.991 --> 00:00:34.562
an owner and a target, and AI Identity
Governance carries AI agents.

9
00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:37.691
Appendix A ties that
to account management,

10
00:00:37.691 --> 00:00:43.687
attribute-based access and least
privilege in NIST 800-53, and to M-22-09.

11
00:00:43.687 --> 00:00:46.490
Now, the part Conditional
Access can't see.
